## Story Description
Upgrade the Category page to surface supplier fragmentation risk without requiring drill-down. Colour-code the L1 bar chart by fragmentation level. When no L1 is selected, show a Fragmentation Scorecard table. When an L1 is selected, add Share of Total and Avg Invoice Size KPIs.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/CategoryPage.tsx
- Import SEMANTIC_COLORS from @/components/charts/constants
- Update l1BarData computation to include a color per entry based on supplier_count: supplierCount <= 2 → SEMANTIC_COLORS.opportunity, supplierCount <= 5 → SEMANTIC_COLORS.attention, else → SEMANTIC_COLORS.risk. Note: SpendBarChart must support per-bar color — check if it does. If SpendBarChart does not have per-bar color support, add a colors?: string[] prop to SpendBarChart that maps to each Bar cell's fill via a custom Cell component from recharts.
- Edit file: frontend/src/components/charts/SpendBarChart.tsx — if not already present, add optional prop colors?: string[]. When provided, render individual recharts Cell components inside the Bar with fill={colors[index] ?? CHART_COLORS[0]}. Import Cell from recharts.
- Pass clickHint={true} to the L1 SpendBarChart to show the drill-down hint
- When isLoading is false and selectedL1Entry is null, render a Fragmentation Scorecard section above the bar chart. It is a shadcn Table with columns: L1 Category | Total Spend | % of Total | Suppliers | Avg Invoice | Status. Rows sorted by total_spend desc. % of Total = (entry.total_spend / totalSpend * 100) where totalSpend = sum of all L1 entries. Avg Invoice = entry.total_spend / entry.transaction_count. Status column renders fragmentationBadge(entry.supplier_count). Compute totalSpend from the hierarchy entries.
- When an L1 is selected, expand the KPI row from 3 to 4 cards: keep existing three (spend, supplier count, transactions) and add a fourth 'Share of Total' card showing the percentage. Apply accentColor to the spend card: supplierCount <= 2 → 'opportunity', <= 5 → 'amber', else → 'risk'.
- For the L2 bar chart when rendered, pass showLabel={true} to show the spend value on each bar
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

