## Story Description
Redesign FilterBar to collapse into a compact pill row by default, reclaiming ~80px of vertical space on every page. An expand button opens the full filter panel. Active filters are shown as removable badge pills when collapsed.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/components/dashboard/FilterBar.tsx
- Add local state: const [expanded, setExpanded] = useState(false)
- Import SlidersHorizontal from lucide-react. Import Badge from @/components/ui/badge. Import X from lucide-react for pill remove buttons.
- Compute activePills array from current filters — an array of { label: string, onRemove: () => void }. Include pills for: date_from (if set: label='From: '+date_from, onRemove clears it), date_to (same), each entry in business_units (label=value, onRemove removes it), each entry in category_l1s, supplier_search (if non-empty: label='Supplier: '+supplier_search), each legal_entity, each currency, each country, each abc_segment entry. Skip any undefined/empty values.
- When !expanded render: a single flex-row div className='flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap py-2': (1) Button variant='outline' size='sm' onClick={() => setExpanded(true)}: <SlidersHorizontal className='h-4 w-4 mr-1.5' /> Filters {activePills.length > 0 && <span className='ml-1 bg-primary text-primary-foreground rounded-full text-xs px-1.5'>{activePills.length}</span>}. (2) For each activePill: a span className='inline-flex items-center gap-1 bg-muted text-muted-foreground text-xs rounded-full px-2.5 py-1': pill.label + an X button (button onClick={pill.onRemove}). (3) If activePills.length > 0: a button className='text-xs text-muted-foreground underline ml-1' onClick={() => onChange(defaultFilters())} text 'Clear all'.
- When expanded render: the existing full filter UI (all current JSX) wrapped in the existing container div. At the end of the filter controls row, add a Button variant='ghost' size='sm' onClick={() => setExpanded(false)} text 'Close ↑'.
- The component starts collapsed (expanded=false) by default — this is intentional so pages start clean.
- Run: cd frontend && npm run build — should succeed with zero TypeScript errors

